config BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_RHKD
	bool "Thingino HomeKit camera (rhkd)"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_RAPTOR
	depends on BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_THREADS
	select BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_RAPTOR_RVD
	select BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_RAPTOR_RAD
	select BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_RAPTOR_OPUS
	select BR2_PACKAGE_FAAC
	help
	  rhkd: native Apple HomeKit camera daemon for raptor cameras,
	  so the camera can be added to the Home app directly.

	  Built on Apple's HomeKit ADK (Apache-2.0), with the camera
	  code ported from HAP-NodeJS. Live view (H.264 and Opus over
	  SRTP, straight from raptor's rings), two-way audio (the
	  controller's Opus played through rad), snapshots, HomeKit Secure
	  Video recording (fragmented MP4 over the HomeKit Data Stream,
	  AAC-LC audio), the camera settings in Home (on/off, night
	  vision, status light), and a Services > HomeKit web UI page
	  with the setup code and QR.

	  Motion sensor (and so Secure Video recording triggers): fed by
	  rvd's IVS motion detection (the default "move" algorithm; IVS
	  object detection is not needed). It must be switched on in
	  /etc/raptor.conf ([motion] enabled = true); until then Home
	  shows the sensor as inactive. The package leaves it off,
	  because [motion] also controls raptor's own recording.

	  Selects raptor's RVD (video and JPEG rings), RAD (audio ring)
	  and Opus support (live view audio is Opus), and faac.
	  Recording audio is taken from a rad AAC output if there is
	  one; otherwise rad's Opus is converted to AAC with the system
	  libopus and libfaac.

	  Installs /usr/bin/rhkd, /usr/bin/hap-setupgen,
	  /usr/sbin/rhkd-setup, /etc/init.d/S98rhkd and
	  /etc/default/rhkd. On first boot it creates a setup code and,
	  once, switches raptor's audio to Opus if no audio output
	  carries Opus (and the substream to H.264 if no stream is
	  H.264), since HomeKit needs those.
	  Pairing survives sysupgrade -B (cfg-backup.list).

	  HomeKit ADK and raptor-ipc are fetched as extra downloads at
	  pinned commits, and mbedTLS 2.28 at its release tag; all are
	  hash-checked.

	  https://github.com/Small6oy/thingino-homekit

comment "rhkd needs raptor and a toolchain with threads"
	depends on !BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_RAPTOR || !BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_THREADS
